  ============================================================================
  CREATURE_RESIZE_PATCH_1. Owner approved 2026-08-23: "nice job on the animals. I
  approve for v1. We'll have to meet them and see how it feels during live play."

  Source of truth: design/Jawa/fauna/CREATURE_RESIZE_LIST.md, generated from
  creature_size_decisions.json (savedBy creature_size_review.html). 25 of 621 cast
  creatures. The magnitudes are DERIVED - drawSize multiplier = sqrt(px / band
  median px), clamped 0.55-0.95 - and must NOT be re-derived here.

  TWO FIELDS, DELIBERATELY NOT MERGED
     drawSize   the picture and nothing else               -> all 23 shrinks
     bodySize   meat, leather, hunting yield, carrying
                capacity, food need, melee scaling         -> ONLY the 2 promotions
  Zero bodySize edits among the 23 shrinks. Shrinking to hide weak art is a
  RENDERING decision; taking meat off a creature because its sprite is small is a
  balance change nobody asked for.

  🔴 drawSize IS NOT ON THE ThingDef, AND THE DEF DUMP DOES NOT CARRY IT.
  It lives on PawnKindDef.lifeStages[].bodyGraphicData.drawSize. The capture reports
  null for all 25 because the dumper does not serialise the Vector2 - so every
  CURRENT value below was read from the mod's own source XML on disk, and the new
  value is current x the approved multiplier, PER LIFE STAGE.

  ⚠️ TRAP, HIT WHILE WRITING THIS: a PawnKindDef block also contains
  dessicatedBodyGraphicData, which has its own <drawSize>. A regex for <drawSize>
  over the whole block returns TWICE as many values as there are life stages and
  produces operations indexed li[1..6] against a def with 3. Extract only from
  inside <bodyGraphicData>.
  ============================================================================
-->
